From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean O'Hollaren <sean.ohollaren@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:54:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FM-1: ENV makes the four knobs attack, decay, sustain and
 release; LFO makes KNOB 1 the wobble

The single envelope knob had one useful step: past it every setting was a click. In its place the
four knobs set the envelope of the music's heard operators one part each, over the rates that can
be told apart in music (attack 6..1, decay 8..1, release 9..2, sustain from silence to full), each
with the instrument's own at the bottom. A sustain setting gives an instrument that never decays a
decay, so that it does something. The wobble moves to KNOB 1 after LFO. Either button again gives
the knobs their first jobs back; EDIT does too, with everything else.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fm1/fm1.h          |  6 +--
 src/fm1/fm1_controls.c | 73 +++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 src/fm1/fm1_web.c      |  3 ++
 src/i_oplmusic.c       | 88 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 4 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 67 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fm1/fm1.h b/src/fm1/fm1.h
